---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const timeline = [
  { org: 'Compute Engine', role: 'Efficiency & Obtainability', years: '2022–2024' },
  { org: 'Ad Exchange', role: 'Auction Optimization', years: '2024–2025' },
  { org: 'Gemini App', role: 'Gemini Live in Chrome', years: '2025–present' },
  { org: 'REVEAL', role: 'Human–AI Interaction, GDM Responsibility', years: '2026–present' },
];
---

<Layout title="Research" description="Research on dependency, anthropomorphism, and socioaffective harms in human-AI interaction.">
  <h1>Research</h1>

  <p class="measure">
    The thread running through my work is a question about what happens over the long
    horizon of a human&ndash;AI relationship: when does reliance on a model tip into
    dependency, when does anthropomorphism stop being a harmless shorthand and start
    shaping wellbeing, and how would we even notice a socioaffective harm forming across
    thousands of ordinary-looking conversations before it became visible in any single one?
  </p>

  <h2>REVEAL</h2>
  <p class="measure">
    REVEAL (GDM Responsibility) studies interaction dynamics in human&ndash;model
    conversations &mdash; over-reliance, dependency-fostering patterns, and related
    socioaffective harms. My work there centers on building the evaluation
    infrastructure for detecting these dynamics: designing and iterating on auto-evals,
    calibrating them against human-labeled data and rater agreement to build golden
    datasets, and pairing that with in-depth qualitative review of user&ndash;model logs
    to keep the metrics grounded in what's actually happening in conversation.
  </p>

  <h2>Prior relevant work</h2>
  <p class="measure">
    Before and alongside REVEAL, I've worked on the statistical and infrastructural
    building blocks this kind of evaluation depends on: applying time-series analyses to
    conversational-geometry features like TRACE signals and embedding-trajectory metrics
    to model how a given interaction dynamic develops across a conversation, and
    constructing the golden datasets those models are calibrated against.
  </p>

  <h2>Where I've been</h2>
  <ul class="plain measure">
    {timeline.map((stop) => (
      <li style="margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">
        <span class="section-marker">{stop.years}</span>
        &mdash; <strong>{stop.org}</strong>
        <span class="muted">, {stop.role}</span>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>
</Layout>
